  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding Distance between Points in R4</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt; Let  \(\mathbf{u} = {@u@}\) and \(\mathbf{v} = {@v@}\), defined in \(\mathbb{R}^4\). &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Find the distance between the points \(\mathbf{u}\) and \(\mathbf{v}\). &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]] &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(&lt;b&gt;Note:&lt;/b&gt;Give your answer in exact form.)&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;b&gt;Worked Solution&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The distance between two vectors \(\mathbf{u}\) and \(\mathbf{v}\) is&lt;br&gt;\[ d(\mathbf{u},&amp;nbsp;\mathbf{v}) = ||&amp;nbsp;\mathbf{u} -\mathbf{v}||. \]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this question we have \(\mathbf{u} = {@u@}\) and let \(\mathbf{v} = {@v@}\) so
\[ &amp;nbsp;{@u@}-{@v@} = {@ws2@}.\]
So 
\[ ||{@ws2@}|| = {@ws3@} = {@ev(ws3,simp)@}.\] 
&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
